From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxime Gréau <maxime.greau@chainguard.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:53:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Skip OpenSSL ENGINE calls when OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE is
 defined

OpenSSL 4.0 removed the ENGINE API and always defines OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE.
<openssl/engine.h> still declares ENGINE_load_dynamic(),
ENGINE_get_default_RSA() and ENGINE_load_private_key(), but only as
removed-API declarations with no symbols behind them, so traffic_server
would fail to link: libcrypto.so.4 from openssl-4.0-libcrypto 4.0.3-r5
exports none of the three (checked with nm -D).

Guard the include and both ENGINE blocks in SSLUtils.cc with
!defined(OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE). With OpenSSL 4 this compiles the ENGINE code
out, as upstream master did when it removed that code in commit
e7eb77a5c3 (released in 10.2.0). The upstream diff does not apply to
9.2.x, where the code is guarded by OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL rather than by
HAVE_ENGINE_* checks. Private keys are then always read as PEM.

Upstream: https://github.com/apache/trafficserver/pull/13471
---
 iocore/net/SSLUtils.cc | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/iocore/net/SSLUtils.cc b/iocore/net/SSLUtils.cc
index f544aa1..26bd00b 100644
--- a/iocore/net/SSLUtils.cc
+++ b/iocore/net/SSLUtils.cc
@@ -58,7 +58,9 @@
 #include <openssl/conf.h>
 #include <openssl/dh.h>
 #include <openssl/ec.h>
+#ifndef OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE
 #include <openssl/engine.h>
+#endif
 #include <openssl/err.h>
 #include <openssl/evp.h>
 #include <openssl/pem.h>
@@ -918,7 +920,7 @@ void
 SSLPostConfigInitialize()
 {
   if (SSLConfigParams::engine_conf_file) {
-#ifndef OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL
+#if !defined(OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL) && !defined(OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE)
     ENGINE_load_dynamic();
 #endif
 
@@ -996,7 +998,7 @@ static bool
 SSLPrivateKeyHandler(SSL_CTX *ctx, const SSLConfigParams *params, const char *keyPath, const char *secret_data, int secret_data_len)
 {
   EVP_PKEY *pkey = nullptr;
-#ifndef OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL
+#if !defined(OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL) && !defined(OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE)
   ENGINE *e = ENGINE_get_default_RSA();
   if (e != nullptr) {
     pkey = ENGINE_load_private_key(e, keyPath, nullptr, nullptr);
